To force a text field to display columns in Adobe JavaScript, you can use the `setRichText` method and the `RichText` object. However, this method is not directly applicable to text fields. Instead, you can use the `setRichText` method on a `RichText` object, which can be created from a text field.

Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

```javascript
var myTextField = this.getField("myTextField");
var myRichText = myTextField.createRichText();
myRichText.setRichText("Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3");
myTextField.value = myRichText;
```

In this example, `myTextField` is the text field you want to modify, and `myRichText` is the `RichText` object that will be used to set the text with columns.

However, if you want to dynamically update the text field with columns, you can use the `setRichText` method on the `RichText` object and then assign it back to the text field. Here's an example:

```javascript
var myTextField = this.getField("myTextField");
var myRichText = myTextField.createRichText();
myRichText.setRichText("Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3");
myTextField.value = myRichText;
// Later, to update the text field with new values
myRichText.setRichText("New Column 1 | New Column 2 | New Column 3");
myTextField.value = myRichText;
```

If you want to create a text field with columns and then populate it with data, you can use the `setRichText` method on the `RichText` object and then assign it to the text field. Here's an example:

```javascript
var myTextField = this.getField("myTextField");
var myRichText = myTextField.createRichText();
var data = ["Column 1", "Column 2", "Column 3"];
var text = "";
for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
    text += data[i] + " | ";
}
text = text.substring(0, text.length - 3); // Remove the extra " | "
myRichText.setRichText(text);
myTextField.value = myRichText;
```

In this example, `data` is an array of strings that will be used to populate the text field with columns. The `text` variable is used to build the string with columns, and the `setRichText` method is used to set the text on the `RichText` object.

Note that the `setRichText` method can only be used on a `RichText` object, not directly on a text field. Therefore, you need to create a `RichText` object from the text field using the `createRichText` method before you can use the `setRichText` method.

